<!-- pg-rehearse:report -->
### 🔴 This migration would have frozen **checkout** for **3.1s**

`demo/migrations/002_index_orders_created.sql` · ran in 3.1s · rehearsed under peak-hour profile, 1,240 req/s, 1 long report txn

| Feature | Normal p99 | Worst during migration | Stall | With safer version |
|---|--:|--:|--:|--:|
| checkout | 4.2ms | 3.1s | **3.1s** | 41ms |
| order history | 2.5ms | 6.1ms | – | 7.3ms |
| order page | 0.8ms | 1.4ms | – | 1.9ms |

**Lock footprint:** Locks `orders` (blocks writes).

**Findings**

- 🔴 `create-index-not-concurrent` — CREATE INDEX without CONCURRENTLY blocks writes to `orders` for the whole build. _Use CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY outside a transaction._

✅ Re-tested: checkout max 41ms, no stalls (migration took 4.9s).

<details>
<summary>Suggested safer migration</summary>

- **create-index-not-concurrent** — Build the index with CONCURRENTLY so writes keep flowing (must run outside a transaction).

```sql
-- create-index-not-concurrent
CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY IF NOT EXISTS orders_created_at_idx ON orders (created_at);
```

</details>

